refresh_0_2_91_to_0_2_93 = All 47 tools/*.json are byte-identical to the 0.2.91 capture — no tool added, removed, or renamed, and no schema (including the update_goal variants[]) changed. prompts/grok-composer-2.5-fast.md and prompts/grok-session-title.md are unchanged. prompts/grok-4.5.md and prompts/grok-4.5-interactive.md both changed in exactly one place: the <output_efficiency> block was rewritten from a "keep output brief and direct, skip filler, lead with the answer" directive (with a bulleted list of what to focus text output on) to a "write like an excellent technical blog post, complete sentences, good grammar, proportional to task complexity" directive — a real shift in the requested communication style, not just wording. misc/grok-composer-2.5-fast-steering.md gained one new bundled skill entry, <agent_skill fullPath=".../.grok/bundled/skills/resume-claude/SKILL.md"> ("Resume or continue work from a recent Claude Code session..."), placed alongside the other three bundled skills (execute-plan, pr-babysit, review); this is a genuine new first-party bundled skill in 0.2.93, not local noise (the other bundled-skills dirs already existed in the 0.2.91 capture). misc/grok-4.5-steering.md is unchanged. One capture artifact was deliberately NOT folded in: the interactive tmux session's misc/grok-4.5-interactive-steering.md capture included a fresh, un-genericized `<system-reminder>MCP server connected: tasks (6 tools)...</system-reminder>` block that this machine's `grok mcp list` shows as unconfigured; tracing it back, both that "tasks" MCP fingerprint and the machine's already-baked-in `~/.agents/skills/*` entries in the Composer steering file trace to a locally cloned `github.com/anthropics/claude-plugins-official.git` marketplace cache and a shared `~/.agents/skills` directory unique to this capture machine, not to a clean/default grok install — so grok-4.5-interactive-steering.md was left untouched rather than baking in machine-specific state.
refresh_0_2_93_to_0_2_99 = All four prompts remain byte-identical, and the tool inventory remains 47 with no additions, removals, or renames. Three tool definitions changed: grok-4.5's spawn_subagent gained an optional nullable model override (inherited by default and ignored on resume); Composer's Task model description now documents fallback to the inherited model for unknown/unavailable slugs and that resumed tasks retain their source model; and read_file no longer claims that lines longer than 2,000 characters are truncated. misc/grok-composer-2.5-fast-steering.md gained two new first-party bundled skills: build-with-ai, which steers AI feature integration toward SpaceXAI, and design, which runs a design-doc author/reviewer loop. Linux OS/shell values, differences in locally installed skills, and the interactive capture machine's tasks MCP reminder were treated as host-specific capture noise and deliberately not folded in.
